.TH POTION 1 "August 2026" "potion 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
potion \- IP flow monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B potion
.RI [ options ]
.I interface
.RI [ expression ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B potion
listens on a network interface using libpcap, aggregates the traffic it
sees into flows, and displays the busiest of them with their average
throughput, as many as fit on the screen. The display refreshes once a
second and is sorted by rate, highest first.
.PP
A flow is identified by the IP protocol, the type of service field, the
source and destination addresses, and the source and destination ports.
Only IPv4 is decoded; everything else is ignored.
.PP
Fragmented datagrams are marked
.B [frag]
in the protocol column. Only the first fragment of a datagram carries the
port numbers, so fragments that arrive before it are accumulated against
the datagram identification and folded into the real flow once the first
fragment shows up.
.PP
A flow is forgotten when it has not been updated for the inactive
timeout, when it has existed for longer than the active timeout, or when
a TCP segment carrying a reset, or both FIN and ACK, is seen for it.
When the table is full, the flow that has gone longest without an update
is recycled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s " " \fIbytes\fR ", " \-\-snaplen = \fIbytes\fR
Capture
.I bytes
of data from each packet rather than the default of 128, which is more
than enough for IP, ICMP, TCP and UDP headers. Accepted values are 68 to
262144, or 0 to capture whole packets. Larger snapshots take longer to
process and reduce the effective amount of packet buffering, which may
cause packets to be lost.
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIn\fR ", " \-\-flows = \fIn\fR
The maximum number of flows to track, 16 to 1048576. When this limit is
reached the least recently updated flow is recycled to make room for a
new one. The default is 64.
.TP
.BR \-a " " \fIminutes\fR ", " \-\-active = \fIminutes\fR
Active flow lifetime, 1 to 60 minutes. A flow is forgotten once it has
existed this long, however busy it is. The default is 30 minutes.
.TP
.BR \-i " " \fIseconds\fR ", " \-\-inactive = \fIseconds\fR
Idle flow lifetime, 10 to 600 seconds. A flow is forgotten once it has
gone this long without a packet. The default is 30 seconds.
.TP
.BR \-S " " \fIfacility\fR ", " \-\-syslog = \fIfacility\fR
Syslog facility to log to. The default is
.BR user .
One of
.BR authpriv ,
.BR cron ,
.BR daemon ,
.BR ftp ,
.BR kern ,
.BR lpr ,
.BR mail ,
.BR news ,
.BR syslog ,
.BR user ,
.BR uucp ,
or
.BR local0
through
.BR local7 .
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-no\-promisc
Do not put the interface into promiscuous mode. Only traffic to and from
this host, plus broadcast and multicast, is then seen.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.I interface
Listen on this interface. An interface argument of
.B any
captures from all interfaces; captures on
.B any
are never done in promiscuous mode.
.TP
.I expression
A pcap filter expression selecting which packets are captured. If no
expression is given all packets are captured. Since
.B potion
drops everything that is not IPv4, passing at least
.B ip
is worthwhile. See
.BR pcap-filter (7)
for the syntax.
.SH DISPLAY
The display needs a terminal of at least 72 by 10 characters; below that
.B potion
says so and draws nothing else. The status line shows the number of
flows currently tracked and, if any, the number of packets that were
dropped or could not be decoded.
.SH "INTERACTIVE COMMANDS"
.TP
.B h
or
.B ?
Show the built-in help screen. Any key returns to the flow display.
.TP
.B ^L
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH PRIVILEGES
Reading packets from a network interface requires privileges, so
.B potion
is normally started through
.BR sudo (8).
Once the capture handle is open and the filter is compiled it needs none
of them, so it drops back to the invoking user for the rest of the
session. Started from a genuine root login there is no unprivileged
identity to return to and it stays as it is.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The terminal belongs to the display, so once it is up
.B potion
reports errors to syslog rather than to the screen. If it appears to be
doing nothing, or exits immediately, check the log.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.B potion
exits 0 when it was asked to quit, and non-zero when the arguments were
invalid, the interface could not be opened, or capturing failed.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR pcap (3pcap),
.BR pcap-filter (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>
